# Editor/OS lock + scratch files (these have been committed by accident before:
# Word owner-lock files, Word recovery files, and *.tmp copies of source files).
~$*
~WRL*.tmp
*.tmp

# Maintenance-tracker planning doc. Carries the full mechanic roster (names,
# Connecteam ids) and the appendix names the probe artifacts as name-bearing
# too. Deliberately kept out of the repo; it was swept in once by a
# directory-wide `git add apps/maintenance-tracker/` and had to be removed by
# rewriting the commit. HANDOFF.md and README.md are tracked and carry no roster.
apps/maintenance-tracker/PLAN.md
apps/MAINTENANCE_TRACKER_PLAN.md

# maintenance-tracker refresh working files. Regenerated on every run from
# Redshift + Supabase; committing them would freeze a snapshot that looks
# current and is not.
apps/maintenance-tracker/work/
apps/maintenance-tracker/logs/

# Operator's GM reference columns on public.locations. Applied by hand through
# the Supabase connector on 2026-09-18, not by any deploy, and the columns hold
# staff names and personal mobile numbers. Reference only -- they grant no
# access, drive no routing, and are not read by any app, so the repo has no
# reason to carry the change and every reason not to invite it into one.
#
# This rule was added once before and lost, because it was left uncommitted --
# an ignore rule that lives only in a working tree protects nothing.
supabase/locations-gm-columns-01.sql
